The review has been written to `docs/reviews/der-catalog/dercat-01-battery-spec-catalog.md`.

**Summary**: 9 findings across 11 products. The most impactful discovery is that Enphase IQ 5P, IQ 5P x2, and IQ 10C all have `round_trip_efficiency = 0.90` (90%), while manufacturer datasheets specify up to 96%. Since `cell_resistance_ohm` is derived from RTE (line 108-110), the 6-ppt gap causes a 4x inflation of internal resistance for these products, over-predicting ohmic losses and under-reporting usable energy — both directly relevant to NEM 3.0 dispatch constraints.
